      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T15:22:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In JGit, `TreeWalk.setRecursive(true)` only enters/skips `FileMode.TREE` (`0040000`) entries; `src.tw.next()` still yields `FileMode.GITLINK` (`0160000`, `Constants.OBJ_COMMIT`) entries for submodules.\n\nIn the full `?recursive\u003d1` response (`toJsonData`), entries carry `\"type\": \"commit\"` and `\"mode\": 57344` so callers can distinguish submodule gitlinks from blobs. Because `paths_only\u003d1` omits `type` and `mode` without filtering `src.tw`, repos with submodules (including `chromium/src`) will include submodule paths in `paths`, contradicting the Javadoc/API docs (\"Flat list of blob paths under a tree\" / \"returns only blob path names\") and potentially causing file-finder clients to treat submodule directories as blob files.\n\nShould this filter to blobs (e.g. `if (src.tw.getFileMode(0).getObjectType() \u003d\u003d Constants.OBJ_BLOB)`) and cover `FileMode.GITLINK` in `PathServletTest`, or is `paths` intended to include gitlinks as well?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 98,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 9999
      },
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "d674fb3feaa50806ed034b43ae34d48f3672b7de",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
