      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T15:22:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that in `WalkResult.recursivePath` (`PathServlet.java:447`), `new WalkResult(tw, path, root, root, ...)` passes `root` (the commit\u0027s root tree ID) as `wr.id` even when `!path.isEmpty()` and `tw` is walking `treeSHA` (the subdirectory tree).\n\nBecause of that, `pl.id` here is the root tree\u0027s SHA rather than the `foo/baz` subtree\u0027s SHA (unlike non-recursive `/repo/+/master/foo` in `treeJson()`, which sets `id` to the `foo` subtree SHA, and unlike `PathList.Source`\u0027s Javadoc `@param id object ID of the tree being walked`). If `WalkResult.recursivePath` passed `treeSHA` as the `objectId` argument when `!path.isEmpty()`, `pl.id` would match the walked subtree.",
